<section class="section collection-section" id="collection"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / CHOOSE YOUR DOORWAY</p><h2>Follow a story.<br/><em>Discover its world.</em></h2></div><p>Read an illustrated story or explore a short introduction. Find an episode by figure, scripture or theme.</p></div><form class="collection-controls" onsubmit="return false" role="search"><label class="collection-search">Search stories<input id="story-search" placeholder="Try Lalita, courage or Ramayana" type="search"/></label><label>Deity or devotee<select id="deity-filter"><option value="">All figures</option><option>Shiva</option><option>Rama</option><option>Hanuman</option><option>Krishna</option><option>Devi</option><option>Sages &amp; devotees</option></select></label><label>Scripture<select id="scripture-filter"><option value="">All scriptures</option><option>Ramayana</option><option>Bhagavata Purana</option><option>Markandeya Purana</option><option>Brahmanda Purana</option><option>Shiva Purana</option></select></label><label>Theme<select id="theme-filter"><option value="">All themes</option><option>Compassion</option><option>Dharma</option><option>Courage</option><option>Protection</option><option>Devotion</option></select></label><button id="clear-filters" type="button">Reset filters</button></form><p aria-live="polite" class="collection-count" id="story-count" role="status">8 stories &amp; previews</p><div class="collection-grid"><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Shiva" data-format="full" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Compassion" id="story-shiva-poison"><figure><img alt="Shiva receiving the ocean’s poison with Bhavani beside him" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/shiva-halahala.webp"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SHIVA / COMPASSION</p><h3>Shiva drinks Halahala</h3><p>When the ocean yields a terrible poison, Shiva acts to protect the worlds.</p><a class="tale-card-link" href="/shiva-halahala.html">Read the full story · 5 min</a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-shiva-poison">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 8, Chapter 7</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Rama" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Dharma" id="story-rama-exile"><figure><img alt="Portrait of Rama, accompanying his departure from Ayodhya" height="768" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/rama-illustration.webp" width="768"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">RAMA / DHARMA</p><h3>Rama leaves Ayodhya</h3><p>A royal coronation gives way to exile, and a family must face the meaning of duty.</p><details><summary>Read the preview<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>On the eve of Rama’s coronation, Kaikeyi asks Dasharatha to honour his promised boons: Bharata’s coronation and Rama’s exile. Rama accepts the forest journey; Sita and Lakshmana accompany him. Their departure begins a new chapter far from the palace.</p></div></details><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-rama-exile">Ramayana, Ayodhya Kanda</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Hanuman" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Courage" id="story-hanuman-lanka"><figure><img alt="Hanuman crossing the ocean toward Lanka in search of Sita" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/hanuman-lanka.webp" width="1536"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">HANUMAN / COURAGE</p><h3>Hanuman’s leap to Lanka</h3><p>Across the ocean lies the next step in the search for Sita.</p><details><summary>Read the preview<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>With Sita still missing, Hanuman undertakes the ocean crossing to Lanka. The journey tests his strength, judgment and resolve before he reaches the city and continues his search. It is one of the central episodes of the Sundara Kanda.</p></div></details><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-hanuman-lanka">Ramayana, Sundara Kanda</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Krishna" data-scripture="Bhagavata Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-govardhana"><figure><img alt="Portrait of Krishna, accompanying the Govardhana story" height="768" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/krishna-illustration.webp" width="768"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">KRISHNA / PROTECTION</p><h3>Krishna lifts Govardhana</h3><p>A mountain becomes a shelter for the people and cattle of Vraja.</p><details><summary>Read the preview<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>After the people of Vraja offer worship to Govardhana, Indra sends fierce rains. Krishna raises the hill and offers shelter beneath it. The account places the community’s trust and Krishna’s protection at the heart of the episode.</p></div></details><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-govardhana">Bhagavata Purana, Skandha 10, chapters 24–27</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Devi" data-scripture="Markandeya Purana" data-theme="Courage" id="story-mahishasura"><figure><img alt="Devotional illustration of Durga, accompanying the Mahishasura story" height="768" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/devi-illustration.webp" width="768"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DEVI / COURAGE</p><h3>Devi and Mahishasura</h3><p>The gods’ combined radiance takes divine form in the struggle against Mahishasura.</p><details><summary>Read the preview<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>When Mahishasura overcomes the gods, their radiance comes together as <a class="glossary-link" href="/glossary.html#devi" title="devī: glossary definition">Devi</a>. Armed with the gifts of the gods, she confronts the asura and his forces. This episode belongs to the Devi Mahatmya within the Markandeya <a class="glossary-link" href="/glossary.html#purana" title="purāṇa: glossary definition">Purana</a>.</p></div></details><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-mahishasura">Markandeya Purana, Devi Mahatmya</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Devi" data-format="full" data-scripture="Brahmanda Purana" data-theme="Protection" id="story-lalita-bhandasura"><figure><img alt="Devotional artwork of Lalita and her divine assembly" height="1600" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/lalita-assembly.webp" width="1200"/><figcaption>DEVOTIONAL ART</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DEVI / PROTECTION</p><h3>Lalita and Bhandasura</h3><p>Enter the sacred narrative of Lalita Tripurasundari and her divine army.</p><a class="tale-card-link" href="/lalita-bhandasura.html">Read the full story · 6 min</a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-lalita-bhandasura">Brahmanda Purana, Lalita Mahatmya</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Sages &amp; devotees" data-scripture="Ramayana" data-theme="Devotion" id="story-bhagiratha-ganga"><figure><img alt="Bhagiratha in devotion as Ganga descends into Shiva’s matted hair" height="1024" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/bhagiratha-ganga.webp" width="1536"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SAGES &amp; DEVOTEES / DEVOTION</p><h3>Bhagiratha brings the Ganga</h3><p>A king’s perseverance brings a heavenly river to the earth.</p><details><summary>Read the preview<span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>Bhagiratha undertakes austerities to bring the Ganga down for his ancestors. Shiva receives the river’s descent, and Bhagiratha leads her onward. The Ramayana tells this ancestral story during Rama’s journey with Vishvamitra.</p></div></details><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-bhagiratha-ganga">Ramayana, Bala Kanda</a></p></div></article><article class="collection-card" data-deity="Shiva" data-format="full" data-scripture="Shiva Purana" data-theme="Devotion" id="story-shiva-parvati"><figure><img alt="Devotional illustration of Shiva and Parvati’s wedding" height="1536" loading="lazy" src="/assets/images/shiva-parvati-wedding.webp" width="1024"/><figcaption>AI-GENERATED ILLUSTRATION</figcaption></figure><div class="collection-copy"><p class="eyebrow">SHIVA &amp; PARVATI / DEVOTION</p><h3>Shiva and Parvati</h3><p>From Parvati’s tapas to the divine wedding: a story of devotion, resolve and recognition.</p><a class="tale-card-link" href="/shiva-parvati.html">Read the full story · 6 min</a><p class="collection-source">Source: <a href="/sources.html#ref-shiva-parvati">Shiva Purana, Parvati Khanda</a></p></div></article></div><div class="collection-empty" hidden="" id="no-stories"><h3>A different doorway awaits.</h3><p>No previews match this combination. Try another search or reset the filters.</p><button id="empty-reset" type="button">Show all stories</button></div><noscript><p>All story previews are shown. Enable JavaScript to use search and filters.</p></noscript></section>
